way of Affidavit Ex.PW1/A has reiterated the averments made in the plaint and referred to the following documents:
(i) Duly attested copy of Registration Certificate [Form GST REG-06] in respect of the plaintiff firm namely M/s Balaji Trading Co., as Ex.PW1/1;
(ii) True copy of Authority Letter dated 19.04.2024, executed by plaintiff firm in favour of PW-1 as Ex.PW1/2 (OSR);
(iii) True copy of the ledger account maintained by the plaintiff firm in respect of the transactions done with the defendant for the period from 01.04.2022 to 31.03.2023,
wherein a sum of Rs.3,65,482/- is being shown as "Debit Balance" as on 06.07.2022 as Ex.PW1/3;
(iv) True copy(ies) of Invoice bearing No.8, dated 01.04.2022, for Rs.10,001/-;
Invoice No.49, dated 02.04.2022, for a sum of Rs.32,200/-; Invoice No.50, dated 02.04.2022, for a sum of Rs.15,880/-; Invoice No.119, dated 03.04.2022, for a sum of Rs.91,501/-; Invoice No.141, dated 05.04.2022, for a sum of Rs.12,900/-; Invoice No.457, dated 26.04.2022, for a sum of Rs.41,000/-; Invoice No.644, dated 05.05.2022, for a sum of Rs.81,000/-; Invoice No.1042, dated 21.05.2022, for a sum of Rs.32,400/-; and Invoice No.1104, dated 25.05.2022, for a sum of Rs.48,600/- as Ex.PW1/4 (Colly);
(v) True copy of legal notice dated 16.09.2024, sent on behalf of plaintiff to the defendant as Ex.PW1/5;
CS (Comm) No.774/2024: M/s Balaji Trading Company V/s M/s SKB Traders: DOD: 04.09.2025 (vi) Original Tracking Receipt and Internet downloaded tracking report as Ex.PW1/6;
(vii) Certificate of Non-Starter Report dated 22.11.2024, issued under the signatures of Secretary,
DLSA, North-West as Ex.PW1/7;
(viii) True copy of order, passed by Hon'ble High Court of Delhi, thereby quashing FIR No.585/2022, U/s 420/272/273/120-B IPC, PS Mangolpuri as Mark A;
(ix) True copy of order dated 11.12.2023, passed by Patiala House Court as Mark B;
(x) Certificate under Section 63 of Bharatiya Sakshaya Adhiniyam, 2023, issued under the signatures of PW-1 as Ex.PW1/10;
(b) PW-1/Shri Anshul Bansal was thoroughly cross

(a) On the other hand, defendant firm examined its Authorized Representative (A.R) Shri Rajender Kumar Gupta as DW-1, who in his evidence by way of affidavit Ex.DW1/A has reiterated the averments made in the written statement and referred to the following documents:
(i) Original Special Power of Attorney, dated 25.02.2025, executed by defendant firm in favour of DW-1 as Ex.DW1/1;
CS (Comm) No.774/2024: M/s Balaji Trading Company V/s M/s SKB Traders: DOD: 04.09.2025 (ii) Copy of Aadhar Card of DW-1 as Ex.DW1/2 (OSR);
(iii) Colour photographs of the products supplied by plaintiff to the defendant as Ex.DW1/3 (Colly);
(vi) Video-CD of the products supplied by plaintiff to the defendant as Ex.DW1/4;
(v) Affidavit under Section 63 of Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023 as Ex.DW1/5;
(v) Copy of complaint dated 30.05.2022 as Ex.DW1/6;
(vi) Copy of Notice under Section 41 Cr.P.C, dated 30.05.2022 as Mark A;
(vii) Copy of FIR No.585/2022, U/s 420./272/273/120-B IPC, PS Mangolpuri was proved as already Ex.PW1/D1;
(b) DW-1/Shri Rajender Kumar Gupta was thoroughly cross- examined by learned counsel for the plaintiff.
(c) Defendant further examined Shri Puneet Kumar, S/o Shri Vinod Kumar as DW-2, who in his evidence by way of affidavit Ex.DW2/A stated that he was the proprietor of M/s Puneet Retails and plaintiff firm had supplied fake, duplicate and sub-standard/inferior quality of goods/food products to him for which he got lodged FIR No.585/2022, dated 24.06.2022, U/s 420./272/273/120-B IPC with PS Mangolpuri.
